IP28 native bring-up (Xiri fork, November 2026)
----------------------------------------------
GENERIC64_IP28 is an N64 R10000 configuration linked at the address above.
Use the ELF64 ip28boot from stand/boot64; the IP22/IP24 ELF32 boot files
cannot be loaded by this PROM. The ARCBIOS64 option selects the firmware
layout and high-address exception-vector path; it is not an IP30 board port.

With console=d, IRIS Indigo2 IP28 (1 GB RAM) boots FFS from WD33C93/HPC3,
runs the native single-user shell, reads and writes files, exchanges packets
through sq0 and halts back to the PROM. The native drivers take over from
firmware after early boot. Physical hardware, sustained DMA/cache workloads,
IMPACT display/input, Xorg and a matching IRIX module are not qualified.

Example PROM settings for a disk at SCSI ID 1:
  setenv SystemPartition dksc(0,1,8)
  setenv OSLoader boot
  setenv OSLoadPartition dksc(0,1,0)
  setenv OSLoadFilename netbsd.ip28
  setenv OSLoadOptions single
  boot
The disk volume header must contain ip28boot as boot, and its FFS root must
contain the GENERIC64_IP28 kernel as netbsd.ip28. Use a separate candidate
disk; preserve the existing working kernel, loader and module as a set.
